            <ArticleTitle>Less pain with epidural morphine after knee arthroplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>447-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Twenty-two patients were randomly allocated to systemic opioids or epidural morphine the first 10 days after total knee arthroplasty. Pain was recorded daily in a visual analogue scale, and knee motion was measured on Day 10. Pain was lower in the epidural group, with no difference in knee flexion or range of motion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
